From 28dfd8b5240190887c19565fb9285d69ec4cb132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:31:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Scan-out as a marker on the GS worker; packets handed over in
 batches

- ga2_pgs::vsync takes what belongs to the tick on the game thread (GS
  registers, stereo setup, flip and game time, the frame's text pieces)
  and posts the rest (flush, scan-out, readback) to the GS worker behind
  the frame's packets (GifArbiter::postTask); the game carries on. At most
  one marker waits or runs: the next one first waits for it, so the EE
  stays at most a frame ahead of the GS. The frame text is sealed in two
  halves: pieces at the tick, prompts (reported by the GS while drawing)
  in the marker (ga2_hitext::takePieces / sealFrame(newFrame, pieces)).
  GA2_GS_SCANOUT_MARKER=0: scan-out on the game thread as before.
- The GIF arbiter gathers packets on the producer side and hands them to
  the worker 64 at a time (or at a sync or marker): one lock of the
  worker's queue per batch. GA2_GS_BATCH=0: per packet as before.
- GA2_PERF: markers per second and time spent waiting for the previous one.

Proof (RTX 4090, gamescope, 4x, GA2_FREERUN, research/run59/gpu-175/proof):
both switches off vs on: the GIF capture (GA2_GS_CAPTURE_AT=0, records and
vsync records) is byte-identical over the 113.75 MB both recorded (530348
records, 966 vsyncs); the frame signatures (GA2_FRAMETRACE_FRAMES) agree
at all 13113 common game times; GA2_PRESENT_SHOTS at 20/45/70/80 s are
identical. English dialogue (Xvfb harness): text, names, prompts and the
typewriter reveal per picture as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
